# Build outputs.
_novo/

# The generated API page.  `novo doc` writes it here so you can read
# what the registry will serve; the registry gets its own copy,
# uploaded beside the archive by `novo pkg publish`.  It is generated
# from the sources, so committing it would be committing a second
# original.
APIDOC.md

# The built package binary — `novo pkg build` names it after the
# package.  This package is a LIBRARY and builds none; the line is here
# for when it grows a `main` and it does.
/form-nv

# novo.lock is committed.  A consumer resolves its own closure and never
# reads a dependency's lock, so committing it costs nobody anything and
# makes this repository's builds reproducible.  It is not on the publish
# allow-list, so it never ships.
